+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry enforces the same JSON Schema it publishes to providers, giving the model a readable tool result when its arguments are invalid.
+
+## Contract
+
+- Static schemas compile at registration and are reused across calls; execution rejects missing required properties, wrong types and enum violations before invoking the executor, returning property paths and constraints without input values in results or logs, while valid input including unknown keys passes through unchanged without defaults or coercion; unknown tool names still throw `Unknown tool: <name>` ([validated by: enforces the static schema before execution without changing input or exposing values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L22)).
+- Function-valued definitions resolve on each execution and validate against the current schema, caching compilation by resolved schema object rather than tool name ([validated by: validates each dynamic definition against its current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L87)).
+- An uncompilable static schema throws at registration with the tool name in the error ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable static schema at registration and names the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L116)).
+
+## Integration and delivery
+
+Validation rejection is a `ToolResponse`, so the existing orchestrator tool-result path returns it to the model for correction within the five-round bound. Executors only receive schema-valid input and may still receive unknown keys. The implementation must document this migration in README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md, .specify/spec.md and the PR body, add a consumer-facing CHANGELOG entry, and make a MINOR version bump. The JSON Schema validator is a runtime dependency; the built package must import successfully. The execute method has a one-line comment pointing here. Output validation, authorization and changing unknown-tool handling are outside this contract.
